# ==============================================================================
# ÉPILOGUE - NOVEMBER DAWNS
# ==============================================================================

label epilogue_november_dawns:

    "How many days have gone by? I've just been reliving this one again and again."
    "…"

    s "Fransk's family is huge, huh?"
    p "Yeah… We can barely hear ourselves."
    m "So many relatives… I can't believe that he lived alone."

    "Lou probably died wishing that his funeral would look like this. But he had no family of his own."
    "Secret services didn't even allow a proper burial, since he died looking like… himself."

    s "Fransk's mom just got done with her eulogy, they're probably leaving soon."

    "As soon as she says that hoards of bourgeois start leaving the cemetery."

    p "Cass' funeral service is up next, right?"
    s "Yeah…"

    "In contrast to the one we just attended, Cassie's service looks much more modest."
    "Her mom's expression is frozen, the perfect picture of shock and sorrow."
    "Around her are some of Cass' friends and old classmates."

    d "You're the one she tried to kill?"
    m "?"
    d "Back in that hospital, she tried killing you, no?"
    m "Yes, that's me."
    d "And you decided to come to her funeral, anyways?"

    "That must be her father, he seems to be aware of what happened that night."
    "His breath stinks of alcohol, he must be wasted."

    d "Still, what a fucking disappointment she was…"
    s "Are you fucking mad? Why would you say that?!"
    d "Frankly, I wouldn't have minded if she just decided to kill those fucking fags. But falling in love with one of them?! That's pathetic!"

    "…"
    "Homos?"
    "Is that how he sees Carm and Fransk? Poor Carm who doesn't even have a body to bury?"

    m "How rotten is your heart? How stunted must you be not to feel an ounce of sadness?"
    d "I'm sorry but she died the day her bitch left us! That witch just removed the spark from her eyes."
    m "You…"
    m "You were the one in charge of her happiness!"
    d "Me? That's a woman's role! Could you imagine? Leaving me alone with her children just because she failed to do her job as a wife? She's the one that's irresponsible!"
    m "You're awful, Kid deserved better."
    d "HA! Kids aren't deserving of shit!"

    "People are starting to look in our direction, the look in her mom's eyes tells me that this must happen pretty often…"

    m "They're your kids, they deserve your love and respect."
    d "Maybe if they listened to me! The young are meant to serve their elders!"

    "!"

    d "All they ever did was complain, complain, cry and cry and cry. So what if I'm pulling your hair! So what if you hate it! Just shut up and o-"

    "{b}*SLAM*{/b}"
    "{b}*THUD*{/b}"

    "His sentence was quickly cut short by Pani's horse kick. There's no getting up from that…"

    p "YOU FUCKING MORON, DON'T EVER GET CLOSE TO HER AGAIN!"
    p "NOT AFTER WHAT YOU DID TO HER YOU DISGUSTING PIG!"
    s "Pani! Calm down!"
    p "Cassie was my friend! This asshole used to…"
    s "This isn't the time…"
    p "!"
    s "Her whole family is watching."
    p "…"
    p "You're the one that should've died, not her!"

    "As Pani gets dragged away by Sthen, her words seem to strike a chord in those that knew him."

    m "You know wh-"

    "I should just shut up. Talking won't bring us anywhere."

    d "{i}*wheeze*{/i} Gh… urg…"

    "Leaving this place might be the best thing to do, Cass' last words make much more sense after meeting this awful character."

    d "{i}*winces*{/i} Come… here… bitch…."

    "Looking back at his pathetic attempt at getting up, there's but a single thought in my mind."
    "No thing."
    "No human,"
    "no monster,"
    "has ever looked more monstrous."

    "…"
    "Some time later"

    m "…"
    "You're Maj, right?"
    m "…"

    "Despite what I've told the police, I don't plan on shutting up."
    "Monsters… as long as they exist, I have to fight for their freedom."
    "Pani, Stheno… I trust that they'll fight alongside me."
    "But first, I have to get someone."

    "Sir, his condition is finally stable. I can't believe he-"
    m "Don't interrupt yourself, I'm aware of the entire affair."
    "Oh! Right! His survival is nothing short of a miracle! If that werewolf hadn't thrown out his arm to protect him from that bookshelf, he'd be a goner!"
    m "Can I see him?"

    "Kid, I won't give up on you."
    "After all, you're the future."
    "He's always been wrong, the elders are meant to protect the young."
    "Kid, no matter what happens."
    "I'll undo the harm they made you go through."

    # [FIN DE NOVEMBER DAWNS]
    scene black with fade
    return